* A global label passed to a macro that uses it as a branch target (b\1 \2 in the body, called
* with ne.s,Lab) or on pc: its local twin, as outside macros (as left the .s branch to the
* global symbol to the linker: "value of -6 too large for field of 1 byte").
* fixed: b864f65 2026-10-11 r68togas: global labels passed to macros for branch targets and pc as twins
* expect text: 4e714e71 66fc41fa fffa4e71
 psect macro_arg_twin,0,0,0,0,0
IfFlag macro
 b\1 \2
 endm
LeaPc macro
 lea \1(pc),a0
 endm
 nop
Lab: nop
 IfFlag ne.s,Lab
 LeaPc Lab
 nop
 ends
